ement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-straddle-closed-set"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-straddle-closed-set"],"id":"long.thm-straddle-closed-set","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.5 (Straddle-prefix closed-set criterion)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.5, p. 46, label thm:straddle-closed-set","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that for every $d\\ge0$ there is a finite support $D_d\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$ such that\n$$\nX_{D_d}(2)\\le t\\le X_{D_d}(2)+R_d.\n$$\nThen $t\\in\\mathcal A$. The supports need not agree at different depths: compactness, together with $R_d\\to0$, supplies a limiting support. Conversely, truncating a support representing $t$ supplies such finite supports. Thus this condition is an exact finite-approximation formulation of membership, not a criterion already known to hold for an unresolved target.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-straddle-closed-set","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-straddle-closed-set","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-straddle-closed-set%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.straddle_all_depths_iff_mem%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-straddle-closed-set%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.straddle_all_depths_iff_mem%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.straddle_all_depths_iff_mem"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2